WEBVTT

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.860
They're coming, Masaru!

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.330
No way, we'd never be able
to beat them all!

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.500
No, I'm going to defeat Faceless.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.620
And save Shirogane!

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.390
Am I destined to lose my way?

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.640
All I want is to have fun in my life

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:49.980
All I want is to be with those I love

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:55.370
Ready or not
Here I come

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.080
I don't care anymore

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.000
I just don't know anymore

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.120
I wish everything would just disappear

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.540
There are days when I think like that

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:11.170
But everything is precious to me

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.380
And so I fight on

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.800
Today was a tough day

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.600
I almost gave up hope

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:27.060
But the truth is I don't want
to lose anything anymore

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.440
I wish everything would just disappear

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.820
There are days when I think like that

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.700
But everything is precious to me

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.950
And so I must fight

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.970
#25 At Mont Saint-Michel

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.720
I couldn't get Masaru because of the fog.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.430
Be sure to capture him.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.180
I want him alive, Naya.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.230
Yes, leave it to us.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.190
Les Derniers Quatre
don't need to get involved.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.740
I hope not.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.700
You two, help her out just in case.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:18.870
Yes, sir.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:24.540
Behold! The numerous trophies
of my ancestors.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.580
The Gundeau family and the Villon family.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.050
All the brave and honorable families
are old friends of mine.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.380
During the Crusades...

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.550
This is all a lie.
Automata have no ancestors or lineage.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.100
Captain Graziano aspires to
those human characteristics.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.100
And believes he's a gentleman.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.270
I heard that elephants are very strong.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.690
So I had one brought for me to fight.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.530
It wasn't worth it.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.530
Brighella is only interested
in martial arts.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.530
Do you know a man named Narumi?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:07.040
I heard he defeats automata
with martial arts.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.290
Is he strong?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.960
Yes, much stronger than you.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.670
Here is the next room, Lady Francine.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.800
How many times must I tell you?
I'm Shirogane.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.220
Arlequino, was it?

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.810
Must we still go visit
these absurd puppets?

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.730
Yes, Lord Faceless requested
that I keep you entertained.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:37.990
I like pretty things.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.950
Clothes, jewelry.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:49.250
And my body,
rubbed clean with human blood.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.470
I'm Lord Faceless's personal jester.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.520
So I won't sing you any happy songs
or tell you any funny stories.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.020
I just stay here like this
until Lord Faceless calls for me.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.450
Are all automata like them?

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.330
Not interacting with one other,
just absorbed in what they like.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:34.420
Yes, all they feel is a desire
to be praised by Lord Faceless.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.460
You too?

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:40.800
To serve you is my only joy.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.470
Joy...

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.800
Joy is to empathize.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.810
Empathize, you say?

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.310
Yes.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.350
Strangers, brought together
under one roof.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:58.610
Learning to laugh and cry together
at the same things.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.150
That process is what true joy is.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.280
And you took it away.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.290
You should've experienced it for yourself.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.120
The joy you feel when kids smile at you.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.130
Is that an order?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.880
Yes, it's an order.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.100
Lise, wake up!

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.360
Masaru...

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.610
Yeah, are you okay?

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.360
Where's Guri-pon?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.990
I don't know. It was all so sudden.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.340
You're right.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.380
-Oh!
-What?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.140
What's that?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.400
Mont Saint-Michel,
an old monastery in France.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.650
Why, Mademoiselle.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.150
It's you...!

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.990
Dr. Lao, the wild beast tamer.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.740
An honor to meet you again.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.030
Wild beasts...

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.120
What are those creatures?
Are they automata?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.670
Yes, they drink human blood
and move with animal brains.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.380
I created them based on
experiments on Beast's brain.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.680
They're my brilliant little babies.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.430
Is Beast...?

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:52.680
Yes, the tiger that killed my sister.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:57.520
Masaru, I was given orders
to capture you alive.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.730
I will need you to surrender.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:00.770
Never!

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.110
Go, Masaru.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.440
Huh? But...

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.780
This is my battle. I must settle it.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.280
Okay, good luck!

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.780
No use running.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:20.500
Well enough, my comrades will capture him.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:24.170
And you, I will feed to my babies.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.930
I can open this door using
Faceless's dismantling knowledge in me.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:59.080
This little piggy had a snack

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.540
This little piggy had none

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.300
And this little piggy cried "wee wee wee"

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.050
All the way home

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.060
I've heard all about you.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:21.190
You're so small and cute,
like a plump little baby.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.860
I'm Colombine, the automaton.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.320
A cute name, isn't it?

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.320
Colombine, one of
the four oldest automata?

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.570
Correct.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:35.320
I lost to the shiroganes in the Sahara.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.830
But Lord Faceless fixed me up like this.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:47.170
I can gather the ZONAPHA bugs
in the air and make them materialize.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.420
If you'll do as I say, I won't hurt you.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.640
Anyway, tell me.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.350
What's in it for you to save her?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.350
For me? I've never even
given that a thought.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.650
Mademoiselle.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.940
Kiss my foot.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.780
And I will let you die easily
without pain.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.530
I'll never lose to you!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.540
After her.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.870
Okay, next question.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.420
Why do humans flock together?

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.960
Because we're weak.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.760
We'd die if we didn't help each other out.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.680
That's why.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:43.350
Automata are strong,
so we can keep moving alone.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.520
There's no need for us to flock together.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.690
But aren't you lonely?

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:55.530
Lonely? Only humans feel lonely.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.870
There is somebody I want to protect.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:02.950
That's why I can get stronger,
why I can change and become better.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.460
Can you change?

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.710
Can lonely automata like you
ever get better?

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:13.710
Shut up. Even if you get better,
weak humans will keep losing.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.720
That's a fact.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.470
Humans aren't made to keep losing.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.520
Humans are still alive today,

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.110
because we pass down what we make
to the next generation.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:33.900
And each generation tries
to make it even better.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.410
Humans have gone through
some awful history, but we're still here.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:44.240
That's because we all try
to work it out somehow.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.920
For the next generation.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:52.500
For those joining the circle
that humans made together.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.590
We want to make it better for them.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.470
So as long as that circle exists,
no matter how small it is...

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.640
humans will never lose to you!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.310
Yeah, but that circle is just for humans.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:12.860
Can my cute little automaton hand
ever join hands with yours?

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.860
There was once a puppet
that joined the circle.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:26.870
She became a human in the end
before she was gone.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.870
I've never heard of such a thing.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.380
You're a liar.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.920
It's true.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.840
Last question.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.890
Are you in love with her?

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.480
You do, that's why you came this far
for her, huh?

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.730
You said there was somebody
you wanted to protect.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.770
Come on, admit it, Masaru dear.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:01.320
I don't know, but I'm going to save her!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.330
Then why don't you try?

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.080
-Is this a trap?
-Not at all.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.080
I'm just curious to see
if you can save the one you love.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.840
Because wouldn't that be so romantic?

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:21.930
You don't have to, you know.
I'm just doing this on a whim.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.050
I'll go.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.050
Then go ahead...

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.190
Then go ahead...

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.490
I came to see
what this junk puppet was up to.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.030
What a disappointment.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.280
Who are you?

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.570
I am Naya Steele.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:49.500
I'm the commander of the android-Os
that guard Mont Saint-Michel.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.460
-Android-Os?
-Right.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.790
The chosen ones from among
the shirogane-Os.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.880
Lord Faceless has given us
the latest bodies.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:02.090
Our original personalities have been
downloaded into them.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:06.850
We are mechanical life forms
that surpass humans.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:14.100
And you're letting a punk go
from our stronghold?

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.770
Go to hell, you antique piece of junk!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.530
That's enough.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.910
For me, you're all the same.
Some stupid squabble between puppets.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.540
What did you say?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:38.710
Oh my, I'm being held by Masaru.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.170
I didn't mean to. I just held my arm out.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:45.300
I'll never forgive you
for spreading ZONAPHA.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:47.680
I'll beat all the automata and Os.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.010
I don't like what I'm hearing.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.720
Saying we're the same
as that piece of junk.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.810
We mustn't break
Lord Faceless's next body.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:01.280
But we can let it experience
a bit of physical pain.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.400
It's going to hurt heaps.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:07.240
We'll let you off the hook
if you cry and beg us.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:08.570
Pain doesn't last.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:14.750
But once a man cries,
his tears never dry up.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:19.790
Interesting. Then you can drown
in an ocean of your own tears.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.140
Physical pain, you say?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:33.430
But you've thrown away your bodies
and forgotten about pain.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:38.350
So why don't I remind you how pain feels?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:40.230
You're defying us?

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.030
-You're Lord Faceless's loyal puppet.
-You traitor!

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:49.910
I can't help it. Masaru held me.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:15:01.790
My biggest dream was to be held
by a human boy.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:06.300
So I'm going to help you, Masaru.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.450
You are human?

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.370
An automaton...

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.000
Human.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.880
What would happen if I did nothing?

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.650
Why...?

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:12.780
Lady Francine ordered us
not to hurt any humans.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:16.410
So I saved you.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.200
That is all.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:24.920
Oh dear, look where we've arrived.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.630
-There they are!
-This way!

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:32.220
Masaru, hold my hand
if you want to be saved.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.430
No!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.650
Lord Faceless's next body!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.190
That too, but this hole is where...

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.580
A parachute for the two of us.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.870
Masaru is safe. Good, we won't be killed.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.340
Fool! Don't you realize
where this hole leads to?

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.510
After them!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.510
Go.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.640
Die where I can't see you.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.680
Get out of my sight.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.190
Um...

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.860
May I ask your name?

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.120
Arlequino.

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:39.370
Mr. Arlequino.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.870
Thank you for saving me.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:54.130
Did you just smile?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.220
Huh? Yes.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.760
-At me?
-Yes.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.930
Did I do something wrong?

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.270
How strange it feels.

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:14.900
I've never been thanked
nor smiled at by a human before.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.280
Gives me strange feelings.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.120
Now go.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.960
Wow, that was so fun.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.170
Are you okay, Masaru?

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.800
Yeah.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.800
This way. Careful now.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.430
Why did you save me anyway?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.810
I already told you.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:50.110
Because I held you? Stop kidding around.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:55.190
This little piggy went to market

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:59.530
This little piggy stayed home

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.120
Hey, Colombine!

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:04.240
This little piggy had a snack

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.960
This little piggy had none

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:12.250
I like that line. "Had none."

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.800
Lord Faceless made me.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.140
And Lady Francine gave me a will.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.270
All so I could make Lady Francine smile.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.310
Yeah, I know.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.060
That's it.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.690
There's nothing else I want to do.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:36.440
I "have none."

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.320
But one day...

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:45.740
I went to a people library on a whim.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.790
And I picked up a random book.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:56.340
The writing was about love
between a human man and woman.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.470
I couldn't understand it.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:05.850
But the way it depicted
how the man and woman embraced.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.230
I was drawn to it.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:13.770
After that, I began to read
humans' love stories.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.780
I loved imagining what it was like
to be held.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.160
It became my only source of pleasure.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:27.950
And you made it come true.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:30.040
That's why I saved you.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.540
Besides, Lady Francine told me
not to hurt any more humans.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.590
Francine? You mean Shirogane?

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:43.340
You want to talk about her again?
Yes, that's right.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.430
Where is she?

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:49.850
See? I knew you loved her.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:54.270
She's the one you want to hold close.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:57.110
Shut up! I'm not even a teenager yet.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.860
I don't have such feelings for Shirogane.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.700
We're here.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.540
What's in here?

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:14.750
The short cut to where you want to go.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.890
This is where the bodies
of the Os are kept.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:33.350
Their original human bodies.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:48.370
This is beginning to get interesting.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.370
That'll keep them out for now.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.090
Narumi.

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:09.850
What we were about to witness next
was the darkness behind the puppets.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:25.200
A past that can't become a memory
plays on repeat

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:29.950
In my mind is a forgotten thing
that I still remember

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.660
Questions remain unanswered
but I must go now

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:39.540
I walk in the dark,
making a promise to my footprints

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:44.210
So many similar beings
leading similar lives

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:48.970
Was there a reason
for me to be born at all?

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:53.720
The world lost all sound
but for the ticking of a clock

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:58.560
A missing heart keeps shouting

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:03.440
A meaningless life was shaking

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:08.030
All because of your unique existence

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:12.660
If the reason for the pain
is revealed someday

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:17.410
If you find a home
for those tears someday

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:22.670
You shall sleep
with the whole universe in your arms

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:30.590
I know it still plays in your heart

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:34.390
The melody that brought you here
